      "cite": "bessel-indicial",
      "prompt": "<ol type=\"a\"><li>Verify that the indicial equation of Bessel’s equation of order $p$ is $(\\kr-p)(\\kr+p)=0$.</li><li>Suppose $p$ is not an integer. Carry out the computation to find the solutions $\\kyone$ and $\\kytwo$ above.</li></ol>",
      "answer": {
        "type": "open",
        "generated_by": "ai",
        "solution": "a) Put $\\ky = \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty \\ka_k x^{k+\\kr}$ into $x^2\\kydprime + x\\kyprime + (x^2 - p^2)\\ky$. The part $x^2\\kydprime + x\\kyprime - p^2\\ky$ is $\\sum_{k=0}^\\infty \\bigl((k+\\kr)(k+\\kr-1) + (k+\\kr) - p^2\\bigr)\\ka_k x^{k+\\kr} = \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty \\bigl((k+\\kr)^2 - p^2\\bigr)\\ka_k x^{k+\\kr}$, while $x^2\\ky = \\sum_{k=2}^\\infty \\ka_{k-2} x^{k+\\kr}$ starts two powers higher. The lowest power $x^{\\kr}$ therefore carries $\\bigl(\\kr(\\kr-1) + \\kr - p^2\\bigr)\\ka_0 = (\\kr-p)(\\kr+p)\\ka_0$, and with $\\ka_0 \\neq 0$ the indicial equation is $(\\kr-p)(\\kr+p) = 0$. b) The power $x^{1+\\kr}$ gives $\\bigl((1+\\kr)^2 - p^2\\bigr)\\ka_1 = 0$, and each power $x^{k+\\kr}$ with $k \\ge 2$ gives $\\bigl((k+\\kr)^2 - p^2\\bigr)\\ka_k + \\ka_{k-2} = 0$. For $\\kr = p$, $(k+p)^2 - p^2 = k(k+2p)$, so $(1+2p)\\ka_1 = 0$ and $\\ka_k = -\\frac{\\ka_{k-2}}{k(k+2p)}$. Take $\\ka_1 = 0$ (it is forced unless $1 + 2p = 0$, and may then be chosen zero); then every odd coefficient is zero. For the even ones, $\\ka_{2k} = -\\frac{\\ka_{2k-2}}{2k(2k+2p)} = -\\frac{\\ka_{2k-2}}{2^2 k(k+p)}$, so with $\\ka_0 = 1$, $\\ka_{2k} = \\frac{(-1)^k}{2^{2k} k!\\,(k+p)(k-1+p)\\cdots(1+p)}$, and $\\kyone = x^p \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty \\ka_{2k} x^{2k}$ is the series above. For $\\kr = -p$ the same steps run with $-p$ in place of $p$; the divisors $k(k-p)$ never vanish because $p$ is not an integer, and they give $\\kytwo$. Check: SymPy reproduces the coefficient of every power through $x^{7+\\kr}$, and the $\\kyone$ series divided by $2^p\\kGamma(1+p)$ gives $\\kJ_{1/3}(3) = -0.0449638$ and $\\kJ_{1/2}(3) = 0.0650082$, the values the software's Bessel functions give."
      }
    },
